    "text": "The rowan is the mountain ash, a protective tree. People tied rowan crosses to the necks of cattle. Elder leaves set on windows and doors turned back fairy power. The tree grows near stone circles and old ruins. People planted it by homes and along property lines. Its wood guarded against witches and the evil eye. A fairy can leave its mark in the dew. People gathered that dew and used it.",
